From 6cc2ec9386cc8706e3e050f316657536b587b899 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:49:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat: K2-Horizon: port the fleet's parser tolerance onto
 upstream's k2-horizon.cpp

Upstream (#29535, b11454) routes every K2-Horizon template to its own
specialized parser before the autoparser runs, so the fork's autoparser K2
workarounds (dropped with this change) no longer run and would silently
disarm the sampler guard. The behaviours are re-derived on
common/parsers/k2-horizon.cpp instead (no shim routing K2 back to the
autoparser):

- every effort's open tag may start the reasoning (repeats are dropped) and
  every effort's close tag ends it; with tools offered the start of a tool
  call (or a complete Kimi-form call) also ends it, zero-width
- the section opener/closer and the call's own end tag are optional, calls
  are always parsed in parallel, arguments are accepted in any order, a
  Kimi-form call is surfaced as a call, whatever follows a call is dropped
- stray close tags / harmony delimiters end the content; tool-call markup is
  dropped when no call can be made
- a "lenient-fallback" rule so common_chat_peg_parse never fails the turn
- feeds the sampler guard (no_empty_reply_inert/hold/open) and
  stops_after_reasoning, and logs one INFO line for the deploy check
- reasoning_format none keeps upstream's raw behaviour

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BidfYiPxg2nUvGVowCgTPK
